  "issues": [
    {
      "id": "ENTITLEMENT_REFRESH_EVENT_COALESCING",
      "severity": "medium",
      "status": "RESOLVED_BY_QUEUED_FRESH_SCANS",
      "file": "Count stick/CountingAccess.swift",
      "lines": [
        145,
        174
      ],
      "finding": "A purchase/update/restore-triggered refresh joins any already-running entitlementTask, even if that task enumerated currentEntitlements before the transaction event and is suspended in subscription.status. The transaction event can then finish without an entitlement scan after the event. A newly purchased user may retain nil expiry and the not-active message until another foreground/manual refresh; a revoked entitlement may remain displayed until another gate refresh.",
      "recommendation": "Invalidate or force a new serialized entitlement scan after verified purchase, transaction update and AppStore.sync. A dirty-generation/retry loop or forceFresh path must not drop events that arrive during a scan. Add a controlled asynchronous regression or verify code structure plus StoreKit purchase/refund/update tests.",
      "resolution": "Each refresh captures the preceding task, queues a separate fresh readVerifiedEntitlement scan after it, and clears the tail only if entitlementRefreshID still matches. Purchase/update/restore can no longer join a scan begun before the event.",
      "resolutionLines": [
        146,
        181
      ]
    }
  ],
  "verifiedByInspection": [
    "StoreKit success and transaction update paths require verified matching product transactions before granting access or finishing.",
    "Current entitlement scan rejects revoked, upgraded and expired transactions. Verified grace-period data is accepted; failed status retrieval does not grant extra access.",
    "Ordinary subscriber entitlement relies on Apple StoreKit currentEntitlements and expiration rather than an arbitrary local unlock flag.",
    "Main-actor shared access manager serializes in-process free reservations; reservation completion is single-use and Keychain is written before publishing results.",
    "Free allowance is lifetime four successful automatic results, including zero detections. Failed/cancelled processing, manual editing and history restore do not debit.",
    "Invalid/corrupt/unavailable Keychain fails closed and can recover on a later reserve; no UserDefaults fallback resets quota.",
    "Denied counting gate preserves existing workspace; saved result view/edit/save/share is not subscription-gated.",
    "Paywall uses localized StoreKit displayPrice, verifies seven-day introductory free-trial period and Apple eligibility, and exposes restore/manage/privacy/EULA.",
    "Scene activation and entitlement expiry schedule refresh. Product errors do not fabricate access.",
    "No network receipt-upload/analytics SDK introduced in reviewed code."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "This reviewer read existing xcresult artifacts and source; did not run or mutate the simulator.",
    "Transactions are Apple local StoreKit Test, not Apple sandbox/TestFlight/production purchases. Physical-device billing and fully disconnected-device behavior have not been tested.",
    "Final current-build screenshot/localization validation, live StoreKit configuration, review screenshot and submission state are separate release lanes."
